    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5df52f13_7bec4900",
        "filename": "include/benchmark.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 68,
      "author": {
        "id": 1534724
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-25T16:24:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The intention here was to:\n\n1. Keep the code as generic as possible, i.e. no need to return a specific type\n1. Avoid error checks inside the performance loop because branches (e.g. `if (error) return ERROR_CODE`) are often slow\n\nMy idea would be that the code under test is validated separately by unit tests, then wrapped around a `void()` function and invoked as fast as possible by the benchmark library.\n\nIn this context, would it still be useful to return errors from the function under benchmark?",
      "parentUuid": "2985fbe7_8deaafc9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 68,
        "startChar": 58,
        "endLine": 68,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "2840be03b49b45fbe2d23471d372d9955303b9ed",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
